# CHG-2067 (approved): the technical publications team signs its readers in with its own Amazon Cognito user pool in
# production's account, which relies on the platform's single sign-on as an upstream OpenID provider (the tech-pubs
# client). The pool is theirs: a neighbour the platform federates with, recorded so the move accounts for it.
dn: cn=tech-pubs-user-pool,ou=bindings,env=prod,cloud=source,ou=environments,dc=ciam-ops
changetype: add
objectClass: top
objectClass: ciamManagedIdentity
cn: tech-pubs-user-pool
ciamBindingRole: tech-pubs-user-pool
ciamManagedService: cognito-user-pool
ciamPartnerOf: cn=tech-pubs,ou=integrations,dc=ciam-ops
ciamProviderRef: arn:aws:cognito-idp:us-east-1:111122223333:userpool/us-east-1_Tp7Rd2Kx9
ciamManagedBy: cn=tech-pubs-team,ou=owners,dc=ciam-ops
ciamChangeRef: cn=CHG-2067,ou=changes,dc=ciam-ops
description: The tech-pubs team's reader sign-in (Amazon Cognito user pool), an OIDC relying party of sso
